Subject: [PATCH] jpeg: don't unwrap the first-row upsample carry in decode_mcu

Defensive: replaces `rchunks_exact_mut(size).next().unwrap()` with a skip
when the raw coefficient buffer is shorter than one MCU row (or the row size
is 0). No input found that reaches the unwrap at the pin: a replay of the
zune-jpeg fuzz corpora (14.6k files) and of ~120k JPEG crash inputs from
other zune-jpeg and image fuzzing runs, plus a 15 min run of decode_buffer,
decode_incremental and decode_apis (6 workers each), all on the pin with
the other suite patches and without this one, found no panic here. An image
crash input that panics in zune-jpeg 0.5.15 at the matching unwrap
(mcu.rs:897) decodes cleanly at the pin, so upstream's buffer sizing
changes since 0.5.15 seem to prevent it. Kept as a cheap guard.

Upstream: the unwrap is unchanged at zune-image HEAD (692520a, mcu.rs:1820).

diff --git a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs
index fd0d808b..802e5749 100644
--- a/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs
+++ b/crates/zune-jpeg/src/mcu.rs
@@ -1103,12 +1103,24 @@ impl<T: ZByteReaderTrait> JpegDecoder<T> {
                             * component.width_stride
                             * component.sample_ratio.sample();
 
-                        let last_bytes =
-                            component.raw_coeff.rchunks_exact_mut(size).next().unwrap();
+                        // Guard against malformed inputs where the raw coefficient
+                        // buffer is shorter than `size`, or where dimensions multiply
+                        // to zero. Both would otherwise panic in `rchunks_exact_mut`
+                        // (zero chunk size) or `.next().unwrap()` (empty iterator).
+                        if size == 0 {
+                            continue;
+                        }
+                        let Some(last_bytes) =
+                            component.raw_coeff.rchunks_exact_mut(size).next()
+                        else {
+                            continue;
+                        };
 
-                        component
-                            .first_row_upsample_dest
-                            .copy_from_slice(last_bytes);
+                        if last_bytes.len() == component.first_row_upsample_dest.len() {
+                            component
+                                .first_row_upsample_dest
+                                .copy_from_slice(last_bytes);
+                        }
                     }
                 }
             }
